A month of a Dutch business account, written the way a bank interface emits
it: SWIFT's transport blocks around the statement, CRLF line endings,
free-text information fields instead of German ?-subfields, NONREF where the
payer supplied no reference, and a month that ends overdrawn — so a debit
closing balance is exercised.

The last :86: stands AFTER the closing balance: it is the bank's note about the
statement, and it must not attach itself to the final transaction.

Opening + the three transactions = closing, and the golden suite asserts it.

